            <ArticleTitle>Paratubal cyst complicated by tubo-ovarian torsion: computed tomography features.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>136-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Paratubal cysts complicated by tubo-ovarian torsion are an uncommon cause of acute right iliac fossa pain in children and very rarely diagnosed accurately preoperatively. We report a constellation of diagnostic CT features in a 12-year-old pubertal girl.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
